From bdd4a584d857485e10c3a22416513be4c2ed1cd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:55:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09358/11362] [outer-loop] Label the h2h substrate, and
 preserve conductor state before stop

Record `gpu_index` on every 6440 head-to-head cell. `server_n_ctx` was already
recorded, so a context change was always visible in the shard. A card-count
change was not: a cell run on one card and a cell run on two looked identical.

On 2026-08-19 that gap became live. The runner passed `--gpu 1`, which
overrides the arm script's own default of "0,1". Qwen3.8-27B fits on one card
at n_ctx 131072 and kept running. Gemma-4-31B does not, and its server exited
with rc=-11 after 14 seconds, so that arm produced zero cells. Had both models
fit, the two arms would have been compared across different hardware with
nothing in the data to show it.

The field is additive metadata. It cannot change what a cell measures.

The conductor state files are committed here because the conductor is being
stopped to free GPU 0 for the gemma arm, which needs both cards at this
context. Commit first, never stash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
